# Brand mark sync

The staircase mark lives in **one** place: `src/lib/brand.ts` (`MARK_PATH`, tile
constants, `markSvg()`).

## Surfaces

| Surface | Source |
|---------|--------|
| In-app sidebar / login | `<Logo>` + CSS `.logo-mark` (real liquid glass) |
| Favicon / tab | static `src/app/icon.svg` |
| iOS Add to Home | `src/app/apple-icon.tsx` → `markSvg({ rounded: false })` |
| Android / PWA maskable | `src/app/icon-maskable.png/route.tsx` → same |

Home-screen icons **cannot** use `backdrop-filter`. Bake the glass look in
`markSvg()` (opaque gradient + sheen + rim). Do not invent a second palette in
those routes.

## When you change the mark

1. Edit `src/lib/brand.ts` only (path, stroke, tile colours, `markSvg` markup).
2. Rewrite `src/app/icon.svg` as the exact output of `markSvg()`:
   `bun -e "import { markSvg } from './src/lib/brand.ts'; await Bun.write('src/app/icon.svg', markSvg())"`
3. Run `tests/unit/brand.test.ts` — it asserts `icon.svg === markSvg()`.
4. Do **not** hand-edit apple-icon / maskable PNG routes for colours; they
   already import `markSvg`.

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Change only Logo CSS and assume the home-screen icon updates
❌ Paste a new SVG into icon.svg with different path/colours than markSvg()
❌ Hardcode hex fills in apple-icon.tsx or the maskable route
```
